  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ClinRC 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'As a clinical trial moves forward, you help collect consent forms, update
    records, and ensure patient information is accurately entered and stored according
    to study requirements.


    <b>As the research coordinator, what is your role
    in this situation?</b>'
  explanation: During clinical trials, research coordinators are responsible for
    managing study documentation and data, including consent forms and study records.
    Their work helps ensure information is accurate and reliable so the study can
    be conducted responsibly and reviewed appropriately. Clear, complete records
    also help protect patient participants and support trustworthy study results.
  correctAnswer: Managing trial data to ensure records are complete and accurate
  incorrectAnswer1: Interpreting trial results and deciding if the treatment works
  incorrectAnswer2: 'Deciding which patients should receive the trial treatment '
  incorrectAnswer3: Revising trial procedures based on early findings
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Clinical
